{"reference":"Judges 6","book":"Judges","chapter":6,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Gideon’s Place in Judges","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Judges 6 begins Gideon’s larger story, which continues through Judges 9. One disputed reading sees this sequence as a turning point: deliverance becomes increasingly entangled with dynastic ambition, idolatry, and violence within Israel. The book’s recurring pattern of crisis and deliverance helps frame these narratives, but its episodes should not be treated as mechanically identical cycles with every stage repeated in the same way.","verse_refs":["Judges 1","Judges 10:1-18","Judges 11:1-40","Judges 12:1-15","Judges 13:1-25","Judges 14:1-20","Judges 15:1-20","Judges 16:1-31","Judges 2:1-23","Judges 3:1-31","Judges 3:7-31","Judges 4:1-24","Judges 5:1-31","Judges 7:1-25","Judges 8:1-35","Judges 9:1-57"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_judges_006_be22c485310bf4e32828581b"],"confidence":"low","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}